  "abstract": "Xin yue lu (信約錄) is a three-bifolium tract compiled by Chauncey Goodrich (富善, 1836–1925) and printed by the Jingdu Meihua Shuju (京都美華書局) in 1894 (Guangxu 20). It sets out six articles of faith (liuxin) and three covenant vows (sanyue), and it retains the pastor–congregation dialogue and ritual directions, which makes it a source for the study of nineteenth-century Chinese Protestant creeds, membership covenants, and terminology. This dataset transcribes fourteen images from Harvard-Yenching Library DRS 428481349, including six text-bearing faces. The AI-reviewed transcription in JSON, TXT, and TEI retains 8 unresolved comparison items and one separately flagged imprint character. Full human collation is outstanding.",
